---
import {cities, nearbyAreas} from '../data/cities';
import type {Scenario} from '../data/cities';
import DealForm from './DealForm.astro';
import {loanTerms} from '../data/loanTerms';
interface Props { cityName:string; intro:string; angle:string; caution:string; location:string; showCityGrid?:boolean; slug?:string; summaryTerms?:boolean; summarySteps?:boolean; scenario?:Scenario; }
const {cityName,intro,angle,caution,location,showCityGrid=false,slug,summaryTerms=false,summarySteps=false,scenario}=Astro.props;
const metro = cityName === 'metro Atlanta';
const nearby = slug && nearbyAreas[slug] ? nearbyAreas[slug].map(s=>cities.find(c=>c.slug===s)).filter(Boolean) : [];
---
<section class="hero" id="main"><div class="container hero__inner"><div class="hero__content"><h1>Fix and flip loans <em>{metro ? 'for metro Atlanta' : `in ${cityName}, Georgia`}</em></h1><div class="hero__rule"></div><p>{intro}</p><a class="text-link" href="#how-it-works">See how the connection works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><DealForm cityName={cityName} location={location} /></div></section>
<div class="trust-bar"><div class="container trust-bar__inner"><span>Built around your project</span><span>Asset-based focus</span><span>Clear next steps</span></div></div>
<section class="section" id="local-market"><div class="container split"><div><h2>{metro ? 'A project starts with the property' : `A closer look at ${cityName}`}</h2><p>{angle}</p><p>{caution}</p></div><aside class="side-note"><span class="side-note__mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><h3>Start with the actual deal</h3><p>Include the purchase price, scope of work, proposed budget and intended resale. A funding partner can then assess the project on its own merits.</p></aside></div></section>
<section class="section section--tint" id="why-us"><div class="container"><h2>Funding conversations that begin with your plan</h2><p class="section__intro">Asset-based fix and flip funding starts with the property, the proposed improvements and the exit plan rather than relying primarily on personal income. A lender may still review credit, experience and other borrower details. We connect investors with possible funding sources rather than making lending decisions ourselves. The <a href="/fix-and-flip-vs-hard-money/">fix and flip vs hard money</a> guide explains how this kind of funding compares to other options.</p><div class="card-grid"><article><span>Property</span><h3>Show what you are buying</h3><p>The address, current condition and contract details give a funding partner a starting point. Include what you know and flag what is still being checked.</p></article><article><span>Renovation</span><h3>Explain the work</h3><p>Share the repair scope and budget you have prepared. If inspections may change the plan, say so up front.</p></article><article><span>Exit</span><h3>Make the resale case</h3><p>Nearby comparable sales and your intended buyer help explain the project. No one can guarantee a resale price or an approval.</p></article></div></div></section>
{summaryTerms ? (
<section class="section" id="sample-terms"><div class="container"><h2>Illustrative loan terms</h2><p class="section__intro">The sample figures used across this site, like an illustrative rate range of {loanTerms.rate} and an advance of {loanTerms.advance}, are placeholders rather than current terms, a quote or a promise. The math behind them, including how rates, after-repair value and fees fit together, is on the <a href="/fix-and-flip-loan-costs/">fix and flip loan costs</a> page. Any lender sets its own terms on the actual file.</p></div></section>
) : (
<section class="section" id="sample-terms"><div class="container"><h2>Illustrative loan terms</h2><p class="section__intro">These sample figures show how a future offer might be presented. They are not current terms, a quote or a promise that any lender offers them. The math behind figures like these is on the <a href="/fix-and-flip-loan-costs/">fix and flip loan costs</a> page.</p><div class="term-grid"><div><span>Interest rate</span><strong>{loanTerms.rate}</strong></div><div><span>Advance</span><strong>{loanTerms.advance}</strong></div><div><span>Loan amount</span><strong>{loanTerms.range}</strong></div><div><span>Term</span><strong>{loanTerms.duration}</strong></div><div><span>Timing</span><strong>{loanTerms.timing}</strong></div></div><p class="term-disclosure">{loanTerms.disclosure}</p></div></section>
)}
{summarySteps ? (
<section class="section section--dark" id="how-it-works"><div class="container"><h2>How the connection works</h2><p class="section__intro">The process is the same in every city we serve: send the project, discuss the details, then review any terms a lender offers. The full sequence and the paperwork behind it are in our guide to <a href="/how-fix-and-flip-funding-works-in-georgia/">how fix and flip funding works in Georgia</a>, and the <a href="/fix-and-flip-vs-hard-money/">fix and flip vs hard money</a> guide explains how this kind of funding compares.</p></div></section>
) : (
<section class="section section--dark" id="how-it-works"><div class="container"><h2>How the connection works</h2><p class="section__intro">The steps below stay the same in every city we serve. The full process, the paperwork a file usually needs and the questions worth asking are in our guide to <a href="/how-fix-and-flip-funding-works-in-georgia/">how fix and flip funding works in Georgia</a>.</p><div class="step-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Send the project</h3><p>Tell us about the property, your proposed purchase and the work you plan to do. You can identify anything that still needs confirmation.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Discuss the details</h3><p>We review the information and may ask for more context. That helps identify whether a funding partner might be a fit for the deal.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Review available terms</h3><p>Any lender decides its own eligibility, terms and documentation. Review the full offer and costs before deciding whether to move forward.</p></article></div></div></section>
)}
{scenario && <section class="section scenario" id="local-example"><div class="container"><h2>{scenario.title}</h2><p class="section__intro">{scenario.intro}</p><ol class="scenario__list">{scenario.items.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ol><p class="scenario__outro" set:html={scenario.outro}/></div></section>}
<section class="section section--tint" id="faq"><div class="container faq"><h2>Questions before you submit</h2><div><details><summary>Are you the lender?</summary><p>No. Atlanta Fix & Flip Loan connects investors with potential funding sources. The lender, if one is available, makes its own decisions and provides the actual terms.</p></details><details><summary>What should I include about the project?</summary><p>Start with the property address, purchase details, renovation plan, budget and intended resale. If a detail is still unknown, explain what you are checking.</p></details><details><summary>What rates or loan amounts are available?</summary><p>The figures shown above are illustrative placeholders, not lender offers. Actual terms depend on the property, borrower and lender. Review a lender's full offer before making a decision.</p></details><details><summary>Does submitting a deal guarantee funding?</summary><p>No. A submission starts a review and possible introduction. It does not guarantee a match, approval or a particular outcome.</p></details></div></div></section>
{showCityGrid && <section class="section section--tint" id="service-areas"><div class="container"><h2>Explore metro Atlanta</h2><p class="section__intro">Every property deserves a local look. Find your city below, then share the details of your project.</p><div class="city-grid">{cities.map(c=><a href={`/${c.slug}/`}><span>{c.county} County</span><strong>{c.name}</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div></div></section>}
{nearby.length>0 && <section class="nearby" aria-label="Nearby service areas"><div class="container"><h2 class="nearby__title">Nearby service areas</h2><ul class="nearby__list">{nearby.map(c=><li><a href={`/${c.slug}/`}>{c.name}, GA</a></li>)}</ul></div></section>}
<section class="final-cta"><div class="container"><h2>Have a property in mind?</h2><p>Tell us what you plan to buy and improve. We will review the details and discuss possible funding connections without promising a loan.</p><a class="btn" href="#deal-form">Submit your project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
